U.S.'s new asylum policy overturned a 2014 decision taken by the Board of Immigration Appeals (BIA) whereby undocumented immigrants fleeing domestic violence could apply for asylum in this country.
U.S. District of U.S. District of U.S. District of U.S. Attorney-General Karl Racine made statements on Friday that the new policy "writes decades of international, federal and state law."
